WEBVTT

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,232
Operationalizing threat intelligence means turning it into defensive action.

2
00:00:05,232 --> 00:00:09,925
A report that sits unread in a portal does not improve security by itself.

3
00:00:09,925 --> 00:00:17,696
CTI becomes useful when it changes a workflow: a detection is built, a hunt is run, an incident is scoped more accurately,

4
00:00:17,696 --> 00:00:26,928
a vulnerability is prioritized, an alert is enriched, an exposure is reduced, a control is validated, or a leader makes a better risk decision.

5
00:00:26,928 --> 00:00:31,237
Detection engineering is one of the most common operational uses.

6
00:00:31,237 --> 00:00:39,930
Intelligence about adversary behavior can become detection logic, telemetry requirements, test cases, and false-positive notes.

7
00:00:39,930 --> 00:00:45,778
The strongest detections often focus on behavior rather than a single brittle indicator.

8
00:00:45,778 --> 00:00:55,164
CTI can help detection teams understand why a behavior matters, where it appears in the attack chain, which platforms should produce telemetry,

9
00:00:55,164 --> 00:00:58,395
and which response action should follow an alert.

10
00:00:58,395 --> 00:01:00,934
Threat hunting also benefits from CTI.

11
00:01:00,934 --> 00:01:08,859
A hunt should begin with a hypothesis, such as whether a behavior described in recent reporting exists in the environment.

12
00:01:08,859 --> 00:01:15,168
The analyst can use ATT&CK mappings, incident lessons, and internal telemetry to shape the hunt.

13
00:01:15,168 --> 00:01:21,246
If the hunt finds nothing, that result may still be useful if the scope and telemetry are clear.

14
00:01:21,246 --> 00:01:24,631
It can validate controls or reveal visibility gaps.

15
00:01:24,631 --> 00:01:29,401
Incident response teams use CTI to scope faster and ask better questions.

16
00:01:29,401 --> 00:01:39,018
Intelligence can suggest related behaviors to search for, likely follow-on activity, affected platforms, and evidence that should be preserved.

17
00:01:39,018 --> 00:01:41,250
It can also prevent tunnel vision.

18
00:01:41,250 --> 00:01:53,406
If a single IOC triggered the investigation, CTI can help responders look beyond that one artifact and consider the broader pattern of behavior, timing, infrastructure, and objectives.

19
00:01:53,406 --> 00:02:04,254
CTI improves vulnerability prioritization by adding evidence of exploitation, adversary interest, affected sectors, exposed assets, and compensating controls.

20
00:02:04,254 --> 00:02:10,793
Not every critical score means the same operational risk, and not every lower score is safe to ignore.

21
00:02:10,793 --> 00:02:19,641
Intelligence helps vulnerability teams decide what to patch first, what to monitor, what to isolate, and what to explain to risk owners.

22
00:02:19,641 --> 00:02:28,104
The same principle applies to incident response scoping, alert enrichment, exposure management, and executive risk reporting.

23
00:02:28,104 --> 00:02:33,567
Operationalization requires ownership, workflow integration, and measurement.

24
00:02:33,567 --> 00:02:35,644
Who receives the intelligence?

25
00:02:35,644 --> 00:02:38,183
Who turns it into a ticket or detection?

26
00:02:38,183 --> 00:02:39,953
How is completion tracked?

27
00:02:39,953 --> 00:02:42,492
How are false positives reported back?

28
00:02:42,492 --> 00:02:44,184
What outcome shows value?

29
00:02:44,184 --> 00:02:55,956
Metrics can include detections created, hunts completed, alerts enriched, vulnerabilities reprioritized, incidents scoped faster, or decisions made with clearer confidence.

30
00:02:55,956 --> 00:02:59,187
Unused intelligence is just stored information.

31
00:02:59,187 --> 00:03:03,111
Operationalized intelligence becomes part of the defense.

32
00:03:03,111 --> 00:03:05,342
Feedback is the maintenance loop.

33
00:03:05,342 --> 00:03:08,343
If a detection was noisy, CTI should learn why.

34
00:03:08,343 --> 00:03:11,959
If a hunt lacked telemetry, that gap should be recorded.

35
00:03:11,959 --> 00:03:19,268
If a vulnerability priority changed because exploitation evidence was weak, the rationale should be reusable.

36
00:03:19,268 --> 00:03:23,807
Operationalization is not finished when intelligence is delivered.

37
00:03:23,807 --> 00:03:27,423
It is finished when the workflow outcome is understood.
